1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,740
 Five, six common tests that we essentially go over.

2
00:00:08,740 --> 00:00:12,880
 And this is all going to be how their athleticism is expressed and how we can get measurements

3
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:13,880
 around them.

4
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:17,160
 So number one, we test out their speed.

5
00:00:17,160 --> 00:00:21,640
 So this is typically a 10-yard dash to be able to test out their acceleration, or you

6
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:26,440
 can just simply do like an overall 40-yard dash, something of that nature, to be able

7
00:00:26,440 --> 00:00:29,680
 to get obviously both acceleration and top speed.

8
00:00:29,680 --> 00:00:33,080
 Number two is going to be kind of more on the agility side.

9
00:00:33,080 --> 00:00:36,100
 So it's obviously predetermined, but we do a pro shuttle.

10
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:37,780
 So your basic five, 10, five.

11
00:00:37,780 --> 00:00:43,040
 We want to be able to see how they redirect force, decelerate, and accelerate.

12
00:00:43,040 --> 00:00:45,160
 Number three is going to be their power.

13
00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:47,480
 We do a vertical jump.

14
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:51,120
 Then the second one is going to be their horizontal force, which is going to be a standard broad

15
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:52,120
 jump.

16
00:00:52,120 --> 00:00:57,080
 Then the other aspect of power that we do test out is going to be their single leg broad.

17
00:00:57,080 --> 00:01:01,840
 After we've gone through off-season training program, whether it be 60 or 90 days, we then

18
00:01:01,840 --> 00:01:07,340
 retest those basic dynamic speed and power movements.

19
00:01:07,340 --> 00:01:11,600
 And then the training should have done the work to be able to see those numbers increase.

20
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:13,280
 Five, six, common.

